    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Nar_Shaddaa"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Clones"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Star_Wars:_The_Old_Republic"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Clone"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Clones"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/class/character"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Cold_War"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Coral was a female human who was once part of SIS Project 32, before she killed most members of the project. However during the Cold War, her sister Mako contacted and met her meeting her, wanting to find answers of her past. Coral attempted trick Mako and her partner into a trap where two other clones of them would mistake Mako for her.
But she was eventually found out when Mako learned the truth from SIS agent Izak, who was also hunting Coral down. Eventually Coral was confronted by her sister and her partner. In the end, she would call Mako a 'cheap copy', confusing Mako of what she meant by that.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Republic_Strategic_Information_Service"/>
