  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Slicing">
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sleeper_Ship_(Lokani_Dawn).png"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Patch_1.0.1"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Crew_Skills"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Slicing is a Gathering Crew Skill which involves accessing secured computer systems and lockboxes to acquire valuable data and rare schematics. Sending your companion to do Slicing missions can be quite profitable, especially if you have multiple companions to work for you at the same time. Taking Slicing, along with a Crafting and another Gathering crew skill, seems to be a good choice for players who do not have a profitable high-end credit making source.
</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/class/quote"/>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Slicing</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Augment"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Companions"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageExternalLink rdf:resource="http://www.swtor.com/blog/crew-skills-game-update-1.2"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Crew_Skills"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Schematics"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Cybertech"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Companion_Character"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Gathering"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Armstech"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Gathering"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Global_Trade_Network"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Armormech"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Slicing</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Nodes"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Synthweaving"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/File:SWTOR_-_Slicing_Tutorial_=_Easy_Credit%27s"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Nodes"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Gathering_Skills"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">Slicing is a Gathering Crew Skill which involves accessing secured computer systems and lockboxes to acquire valuable data and rare schematics. Sending your companion to do Slicing missions can be quite profitable, especially if you have multiple companions to work for you at the same time. Taking Slicing, along with a Crafting and another Gathering crew skill, seems to be a good choice for players who do not have a profitable high-end credit making source.
Slicing is currently the most profitable gathering skill, producing profit in actual credits for almost every mission you send your companion on. However, with Patch 1.0.1, the rewards have been reduced. Players have yet to determine the overall effects of the change. When doing missions, you can pick between augment missions or lockbox missions. Lockbox missions are the profitable ones, and yield credit boxes often containing many more credits in them than you spent on the mission. However, slicing doesn't yield any crafting materials so players interested in crafting will have to buy their materials from other players on the Global Trade Network . In many players' minds slicing is only a crew skill to use until they reach level 50. Utilizing slicing in this manner will add a large supplemental income on the side with very little effort. If you plan on using Slicing make sure you are running multiple missions at a time with more than 1 companion. It is worth noting that Augment missions are usually not profitable, since their only use during leveling is to be placed into an "Augment slot" that is only found in exceptionally crafted gear pieces - which are quite rare during leveling.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">slicing</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Slicing</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Companions"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Crafting_Skills"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Crew_Skills"/>
  </rdf:Description>
