  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Rajivari">
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Dark_Jedi"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Fount of Rajivari</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns1:class rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Unknown</ns1:class>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Rajivari</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Rajivari</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Jedi"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Jedi_Masters"/>
    <ns1:race rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Human"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Rajivari was a male human Jedi Master and one of the founders of the Jedi Order, but he was displeased with what the other founders were molding the order into. Rajivari gathered an army of force users and trained them to use as an army to help him change the Jedi order.
The army failed and Rajivari died but remained as a force ghost, he became "The Fount of Rajivari" a archive of all rajivari's power and knowledge, At one point Rajivari met Nalen Raloch, a Twi'lek who wanted to destroy the Jedi Order, Rajivari gave Nalen his knowledge and power but then realized that Nalen was crazy and wanted to destroy the jedi order not rebuild it like Rajivari himself wanted, because of this Rajivari told the young jedi consular who came soon after, where Nalen Raloch had gone, to prevent him from destroying the ancient lightsaber forge.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Swtor_2014-12-06_13-12-35-12.png"/>
