  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Lost_Jedi">
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Lost Jedi</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Jedi_Civil_War"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Jedi_Order"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Jedi_Order"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Jedi_General"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">The Lost Jedi is a name given to the group of Jedi who survived the Jedi Civil War and withdrew from the Galaxy during the Jedi Purge.
The most notable of the Lost Jedi was the Jedi Exile, Meetra Surik, a former Jedi General exiled for her actions during the Mandalorian Wars, who was ultimately responsibly for defeating the remnants of the Sith Empire and trained multiple apprentices that would go on to rebuild and lead the Jedi Order after she disappeared from Republic space to find and join Revan in his hunt for the True Sith.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Vandar_Tokare"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Lost Jedi</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Sith_Empire"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Darth_Sion"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/class/wookieepedia"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Lost Jedi is a name given to the group of Jedi who survived the Jedi Civil War and withdrew from the Galaxy during the Jedi Purge.
The most notable of the Lost Jedi was the Jedi Exile, Meetra Surik, a former Jedi General exiled for her actions during the Mandalorian Wars, who was ultimately responsibly for defeating the remnants of the Sith Empire and trained multiple apprentices that would go on to rebuild and lead the Jedi Order after she disappeared from Republic space to find and join Revan in his hunt for the True Sith.

</rdfs:comment>
