    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Strongholds"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">Strongholds are fully customizable apartments that can be purchased by players and decorated to a player's liking. Bound to legacy upon purchase, strongholds can be accessed by anyone in the same legacy, even characters that belong to the opposite faction (depending on the stronghold). Stronghold listings were initially only available for four planets across all servers: Coruscant, Dromund Kaas, Nar Shaddaa and Tatooine. Three more were added with later updates: Yavin 4, Manaan, and the special Umbara Mobile Base. Note that the Umbara Mobile base is rather unique in the way it is made available for players.
Originally, only four strongholds per legacy could be active at any time. Then, after a server merger update, seemingly all the active strongholds a player owned, across the particular set of server that were merged could be active. This meant that theoretically one could have approximately 12 active strongholds per legacy, including up to 3 different versions of each stronghold, provided these were owned prior to the merger. 
In order to use a new stronghold (over the imposed limit), one of the active ones must be deactivated. All decorations inside the deactivated stronghold will automatically be moved into the decorations list to be made available somewhere else, but otherwise it will remain the same. When purchased with credits, reactivation costs the same amount as the purchase price; when purchased with Cartel Coins, reactivation is free.
During anniversary events, Coruscant Apartment/Kaas City Apartment are usually offered on sale to Level 10+ players for a pittance representing the anniversary year (i.e. five credits on the fifth anniversary).
In order to purchase the Umbara Mobile Base, a player must run Crisis on Umbara to earn 60 Alliance Recon Data. They must also purchase the Invitation: Trader’s Quarters from the Recovered Goods Vendor in the Alliance Supply Area on Odessen for the Alliance Recon Data and an additional 10,000 Credits. 
Strongholds can be purchased for personal creativity or can be obtained and customized by a guild for a much higher price. This format is similar to guild flagships.
Purchasing a stronghold can happen in two different ways:Travel to Carrick Station/Vaiken Spacedock and find the terminals in the Strongholds/Crew Skills sectionTravel to the planet of choice and locate the terminalCoruscant - Senate Plaza Marketplace underneath the Senate Plaza, terminals located on either sideDromund Kaas - Kaas City Marketplace, either side of main walkwayNar Shaddaa - Two terminals located on Republic and Imperial sections of the Lower PromenadeTatooine - Just inside the spaceport (both factions)

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Kaas_City"/>
  </rdf:Description>
