  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Zayne_Carrick">
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Phaeda"/>
    <ns1:class rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Jedi_Guardian_(Advanced_Class)"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Zayne Carrick</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Jedi_Sentinel"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Unifying_Force"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Lucien_Draay"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Humans"/>
    <ns1:cstyle rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Telekinesis"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Zayne Carrick was a male Human Jedi Padawan later Jedi Knight during the Mandalorian Wars. Born with only a marginal connection to the Force, Zayne spent most of his time among the Jedi fully expecting to wash out someday. Despite this lack of raw ability, Zayne tried his best and did show a talent for making friends as well as a strong understanding of Jedi ideals.
Those ideals were put to the test when he found himself framed for murder by his own master Lucien Draay. While on the run Zayne found his destiny to be tied to his friend Alek; the man who would someday become Darth Malak.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns1:status rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Deceased</ns1:status>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Humans"/>
