    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Sith_Lord"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Codex"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Ajunta_Pall"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Game_sublevels"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Star_Wars:_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Tomb of Ajunta Pall</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Sith_artifacts"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Star_Wars:_The_Old_Republic"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">The Tomb of Ajunta Pall was the final resting place of the Sith Lord Ajunta Pall. It was located in the Valley of the Dark Lords and excavated shortly after the Sith Academy was set up at the entrance to the valley.
In the inner chamber of the tomb, where Pall's body actually rests, there are three swords: a double-bladed sword, a silver-lined sword, and a red vibroblade. One of these blades is Ajunta Pall's Sword.
The Sith Lord's Force ghost still abides in the inner chamber of the tomb.
The Tomb is also a low-level mission area for Sith Warrior and Sith Inquisitor.

</ns5:abstract>
