    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:NPCs/Deceased_NPCs"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Mandalorian"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Jogo</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Jogo or also known as Jogo the Carver was a male Human Mandalorian warrior who lived during the Cold War. On Dromund Kaas, he and several other Mandalorians came to the The Wilds to test themselves against Sithspawn there. However the The Grand Champion came to their camp, to get info on the Sithspawn. Jogo believed the Hunter would not survive the encounter, but was proven wrong, he accepted the Champion's victory and he and rest of his men cheered the hunter on. He was briefly seen on Taris, giving a report to Commander Vorten Fett.
Jogo was last seen on the Taris Orbital Station, over seeing the exchange between Jicoln Cadera and the Grand Hunt Champion. After Torian Cadera said he will join the Champion, Jogo told him try make something of himself and called him 'aru'tal' but not with some kind of disrespect as before.

</ns5:abstract>
