  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Tuk%27ata">
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/The_Force"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Codex"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Tuk'ata have three rows of teeth, sharp claws and horns. They are unusually intelligent and capable of communicating with one another. They can recognize Force users and attack them with ferocity. These creatures were once bred for training purposes, but have long since become guardians for the old tombs on Korriban. During the Cold War, the Tuk'ata were used for researching The Force and its capabilities by a Sith named Renning.

</rdfs:comment>
    <ns5:thumbnail rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Swtor_2014-10-18_13-39-21-63.png?width=300"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Tuk'ata</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Bestiary"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Renning"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/File:Swtor_2014-10-18_13-39-21-63.png"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Codex"/>
    <ns5:thumbnail rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Attack_of_the_Tuk%27ata.jpg?width=300"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Tuk'ata</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Bestiary"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">Tuk'ata have three rows of teeth, sharp claws and horns. They are unusually intelligent and capable of communicating with one another. They can recognize Force users and attack them with ferocity. These creatures were once bred for training purposes, but have long since become guardians for the old tombs on Korriban. During the Cold War, the Tuk'ata were used for researching The Force and its capabilities by a Sith named Renning.

</ns5:abstract>
