    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Lightsabers"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Double-bladed lightsaber</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">A Double-bladed lightsaber, also known as a saberstaff, is a weapon used by the Sith Assassin and the Jedi Shadow.
Contrary to popular belief, the saberstaff is not simply two lightsabers joined at the pommel, although it is possible that some have been created in this manner. Satele Shan's saberstaff was at one point cleaved in two by Darth Malgus, and the saberstaff became instantly disabled as a result. A saberstaff can also be used with only one blade extended, or the two blades can be extended simultaneously.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:thumbnail rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jaesa_(Saberstaff).jpg?width=300"/>
    <ns5:thumbnail rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Darth_vindican_in_combat.jpg?width=300"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Jedi_Shadow_(title)"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A Double-bladed lightsaber, also known as a saberstaff, is a weapon used by the Sith Assassin and the Jedi Shadow.
Contrary to popular belief, the saberstaff is not simply two lightsabers joined at the pommel, although it is possible that some have been created in this manner. Satele Shan's saberstaff was at one point cleaved in two by Darth Malgus, and the saberstaff became instantly disabled as a result. A saberstaff can also be used with only one blade extended, or the two blades can be extended simultaneously.

</rdfs:comment>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Vodo-Siosk_Baas"/>
