    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">So you have decided to be a 'fixer' for the Empire by playing an Imperial Agent. With surgical strikes and stealthy maneuvering the Republic won't know what hit them. So, let's get started!To start with, though their storylines are somewhat similar, the two advanced classes of the agent (Sniper and Operative) play very differently. The Operative can stealth up, which is immensely powerful in the ability to choose/time your fights. But then, the Operative's most powerful attacks are short range, and so this surprise is necessary for survival. The Sniper has the powerful long-ranged attacks but lacks the stealth.</rdfs:comment>
