  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Flesh_Eating_Baby">
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Flesh Eating Baby</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Guid"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Missions"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Tython_Missions"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Flesh Eating Baby</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Flesh_Raider"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Tython_Missions"/>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/First_Responder.png"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Tython"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">While traveling through Tython, you happened upon a Flesh Raider corpse and noticed something moving in its backpack. You checked the backpack and found a Flesh Raider child. The child was alive and friendly, but obviously starved. Master Quilb at the Jedi Temple would care for the child, but it will not survive a trip to the temple without food. 
There are several guid roaming the area that might provide a meal for the child. Kill guid along the mountain path and harvest their meat.

</ns5:abstract>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">While traveling through Tython, you happened upon a Flesh Raider corpse and noticed something moving in its backpack. You checked the backpack and found a Flesh Raider child. The child was alive and friendly, but obviously starved. Master Quilb at the Jedi Temple would care for the child, but it will not survive a trip to the temple without food. 
There are several guid roaming the area that might provide a meal for the child. Kill guid along the mountain path and harvest their meat.

</rdfs:comment>
