    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Tython"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Kolovish was the first Matriarch of the Twi'lek Pilgrims on Tython. She guided the Pilgrims from their homeworld to Tython and she is retired as a matriarch as soon as the settlement was firmly esablished. She spent her time far from the settlement upon relinquishing her power and is overseeing rites for Jedi Padawans.
</rdfs:comment>
    <ns5:thumbnail rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kolovish.png?width=300"/>
    <ns1:strength rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Regular</ns1:strength>
    <ns5:wikiPageExternalLink rdf:resource="http://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Black_Codex"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Kolovish was the first Matriarch of the Twi'lek Pilgrims on Tython. She guided the Pilgrims from their homeworld to Tython and she is retired as a matriarch as soon as the settlement was firmly esablished. She spent her time far from the settlement upon relinquishing her power and is overseeing rites for Jedi Padawans.
After her retirement, Kolovish was discovered to be a member of the galaxy-spanning organization known as The Star Cabal . She was one of the more influential members, as she was station on Tython, the homeworld of the Jedi Order. Because the Cabal hates both Jedi and Sith alike, they recruited her to their organization in the hopes of eventually getting the drop on the Jedi from the inside. She was discovered, but not recognized, by an Imperial cipher agent after the disbanding of Imperial Intelligence. Her connections to the Cabal dissolved upon the agent's retrieval of the Black Codex, the Cabal's storage computer for all their connections. Now, she continues to aid Tython's Jedi Padawans, while trying to keep in tough with the other members of the dissolved Cabal and reform it from the ashes.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Padawan"/>
    <ns1:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Kolovish</ns1:name>
    <ns1:level rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14</ns1:level>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Mola_Haxtor">
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Females"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">{{ #if: |
Mola Haxtor was a Human female geneticist and scientist who studied the Rakghouls on Taris during the Cold War between the Galactic Republic and Sith Empire. 
During the conflict, she was captured by the Empire and forced to release all her secrets of the plague under torture by Sith interrogators. While tortured, her cell was visited by an enforcer of Darth Gravus, who made her reveal information she had uncovered about the Nekghoul variant and a Jedi Master, Sulan, who was trying to shepherd them toward the light side of the Force.

</rdfs:comment>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Females"/>
