  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Republic_Embassy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Sith"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Star_Wars:_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">The Republic Embassy is a section of Manaan on, where Revan and his party learn of strange happenings on the planet.
When Revan first arrives at the Embassy, he is asked by Roland Wann, the ambassador if he can infiltrate the Sith Embassy and recover a lost data module from a probe droid that was sent to investigate trouble down in a secret facility on the edge of the Hrakert Rift and damaged, then recovered by the Sith.
After Revan returns, he is requested to investigate disturbances at the facility and fix them, either by poisoning a giant firaxan shark or by destroying the machinery that seems to be aggravating it.
The Embassy has a computer room, holding cells, a submersible launch bay, and a reception room.

</ns5:abstract>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/SWTORHUB_FPMR_05.jpg"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Republic Embassy</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Star_Wars:_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_planets"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Republic Embassy</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The Republic Embassy is a section of Manaan on, where Revan and his party learn of strange happenings on the planet.
When Revan first arrives at the Embassy, he is asked by Roland Wann, the ambassador if he can infiltrate the Sith Embassy and recover a lost data module from a probe droid that was sent to investigate trouble down in a secret facility on the edge of the Hrakert Rift and damaged, then recovered by the Sith.
</rdfs:comment>
