  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Social_Points">
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Codex"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Codex"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This article discusses the SW:TOR in-game system that measures and tracks a character's social, or multiplayer, interactions. 
Social points can be earned through talking with a large group of players, doing a storyline for other players (note that the person who initiated the quest will not get social points) or participating in dungeons with groups. The larger the group, the more social points each person earns.

</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/class/quote"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Points</rdfs:label>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Points</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Social_Armor"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Star_Wars:_The_Old_Republic"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Points</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Game_Mechanics"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Game_Rules"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Game_Mechanics"/>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Social_VossMystic_Male.png"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Social_Armor"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">This article discusses the SW:TOR in-game system that measures and tracks a character's social, or multiplayer, interactions. 
Social points can be earned through talking with a large group of players, doing a storyline for other players (note that the person who initiated the quest will not get social points) or participating in dungeons with groups. The larger the group, the more social points each person earns.

</ns5:abstract>
  </rdf:Description>
