  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/The_Black_Talon/Conversations">
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Flashpoint_Conversations"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">The Black Talon/Conversations</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">Lieutenant Sylas (to Imperial Lieutenant): Well, tell the captain that I'll be back on the bridge as soon as I've done his errand.Imperial Lieutenant (to Lieutenant Sylas): Yes, sir.
Lieutenant Sylas (to group): Good to have you aboard. I'm Lieutenant Sylas, second-in-command of the Black Talon; we're your ride to Dromund Kaas.1.Very GoodPlayer: I'm sure the ship will suffice. How long until we reach the planet?Lieutenant Sylas: Shouldn't be mnore than a day. The Black Talon makes this run a regular basis without much trouble. We're primarily a transport.2. Hello, Lieutenant
Player Well met and all that.Lieutenant Sylas: Indeed. Welcome-it's not a comfortable ship, but as transports go, it does its job. On our present course, we should arrive at the capital within a day. Won't be any trouble.3. This is my welcome?
Player: Is there a reason your captain isn't bothering to greet me?Lieutenant Sylas: We may only be a transport, but someone need to stay on the bridge-and the captain prefers to keep to himself. On our present course, we should arrive at the capital within a day. Won't be any trouble.
Lieutenant Sylas: In the meantime, your droid's in the conference room. We picked it up with the upgrades from Geonosis; when we docked here, it mentioned your name.1. Droid?Player: Sorry, I don't know what droid you're talking about.Lieutenant Sylas: Oh? The machine asked for you, so I assumed you were the owner. My mistake.Lieutenant Sylas: In any case, it seems that someone wants to get in touch. The conference room is down the hall; I'll be on the bridge.2.There's some mistake.Player: You got the wrong person.Lieutenant Sylas: Oh? The machine asked for you, so I assumed you were the owener. My mistake.Lieutenant Sylas: In any case, it seems that someone wants to get in touch. The conference room is down the hall; I'll be on the bridge.3. If you say so....Player: If my droid's waiting, then I should go see what it wants.Lieutenant Sylas: Feel free to bother the crew if you need anything else. I'll be on the bridge.
Lieutenant Sylas (to Imperial Marine): And you, solider--when you're done playing honour guard, get back to your post. This isn't a luxury yacht. Imperial Marine (in response): Yes, sir!</ns5:abstract>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">The Black Talon/Conversations</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Swtor_2014-12-06_17-18-41-78.png"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">talk to</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Lieutenant Sylas (to Imperial Lieutenant): Well, tell the captain that I'll be back on the bridge as soon as I've done his errand.Imperial Lieutenant (to Lieutenant Sylas): Yes, sir.
Lieutenant Sylas (to group): Good to have you aboard. I'm Lieutenant Sylas, second-in-command of the Black Talon; we're your ride to Dromund Kaas.1.Very GoodPlayer: I'm sure the ship will suffice. How long until we reach the planet?Lieutenant Sylas: Shouldn't be mnore than a day. The Black Talon makes this run a regular basis without much trouble. We're primarily a transport.2. Hello, Lieutenant
</rdfs:comment>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Flashpoint_Conversations"/>
