  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Rodia">
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Rodia</rdfs:label>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Outer_Rim_Planets"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Galactic_Senate"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Rodian"/>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Rodia</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Outer_Rim_Planets"/>
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Planets"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">Rodia is a rainforested and industrial planet found in the Tyrius system in the Outer Rim and was the homeworld of the Rodian species.
Rodia is a hot and humid world which was covered in dense tropical jungles as well as sprawling cities, swamps and industrial areas. A large area of the planet is also covered in oceans and there appeared to be two polar regions on the extreme latitudes.
The Rodians built their cities on waterways and protected them with environmental shields, bubble domes that surrounded all habitation structures and allowed entry and exit for vehicles and vessels. These domes also protect from the extreme temperatures of the planet.</ns5:abstract>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Rodia</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Rodia is a rainforested and industrial planet found in the Tyrius system in the Outer Rim and was the homeworld of the Rodian species.
Rodia is a hot and humid world which was covered in dense tropical jungles as well as sprawling cities, swamps and industrial areas. A large area of the planet is also covered in oceans and there appeared to be two polar regions on the extreme latitudes.
</rdfs:comment>
