  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Ewok">
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Treek"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/class/species"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Ewok</rdfs:label>
    <ns5:thumbnail rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/BountyHuntingTreek.png?width=300"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Ewoks were sentient, diminutive, furry bipeds native to Endor. Ewoks were curious individuals that stood about one meter tall. Although extremely skilled in forest survival and the construction of primitive technology like hang gliders and catapults, the Ewoks had yet to progress past stone-level technology and rely on spears, slings, and knives as weapons.
Ewok culture is tribal and superstitious. Many of their rigid customs are based on superstitious folklore told by their shaman.

</rdfs:comment>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Ewok</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Endor"/>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/BountyHuntingTreek.png"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/File:BountyHuntingTreek.png"/>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">Ewoks were sentient, diminutive, furry bipeds native to Endor. Ewoks were curious individuals that stood about one meter tall. Although extremely skilled in forest survival and the construction of primitive technology like hang gliders and catapults, the Ewoks had yet to progress past stone-level technology and rely on spears, slings, and knives as weapons.
Ewok culture is tribal and superstitious. Many of their rigid customs are based on superstitious folklore told by their shaman.

</ns5:abstract>
