  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Social_Hubs">
    <ns6:subject rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Gameplay"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/class/reflist"/>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLink rdf:resource="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Category:Gameplay"/>
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Hubs</ns4:altLabel>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Social Hubs</rdfs:label>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Snivvian.jpg"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">These locations help promote the teamwork that some players find most enjoyable in MMORPGs.
Hub locations can also be pivotal for completing certain game events. These hubs provide access to Flashpoints and Operations. Starting the event is sometimes framed as entering a drop ship from the hub location.
Examples of social hubs include Vaiken Spaceport and Carrick Space Station.

</rdfs:comment>
    <ns5:abstract xml:lang="en">These locations help promote the teamwork that some players find most enjoyable in MMORPGs.
Hub locations can also be pivotal for completing certain game events. These hubs provide access to Flashpoints and Operations. Starting the event is sometimes framed as entering a drop ship from the hub location.
Examples of social hubs include Vaiken Spaceport and Carrick Space Station.

</ns5:abstract>
  </rdf:Description>
