  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbkwik.webdatacommons.org/swtor.wikia.com/resource/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_3">
    <ns4:altLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Kotor 3</ns4:altLabel>
    <ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Knights of the Old Republic 3</ns5:wikiPageWikiLinkText>
    <ns1:content rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Knights of the Old Republic 3 was the cancelled third installment of the Knights of the Old Republic series of Star Wars video games.

Set after the events of Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords, the game would've had players visiting the planets Coruscant, Mandalore, Rodia and Taloraan as well as an unknown female character named Naresha.

Confirmed crew of the project include John Stafford , Molly Denmark  and Corey Allemeier . According to Stafford about the development of the game, "we got quite a bit of traction... we wrote a story, designed most of the environments/worlds, and many of the quests, characters, and items." Eventually the project was cancelled when LucasArts had a difficult financial period.

In 2008, concept artwork and details about the game was published in the book Rogue Leaders: The Story of LucasArts by Rob Smith, and published by Chronicle Books.
External links</ns1:content>
    <ns3:depiction rdf:resource="http://swtor.wikia.com/wiki/Special:FilePath/Korriban_Orbital_security_station.jpg"/>
    <ns1:images rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic series</ns1:images>
    <ns1:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic 3</ns1:title>
